_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 6
---
order: 6
---
short_label: V.6
---
statement: If two magnitudes are equimultiples of two magnitudes, and any magnitudes subtracted from them are equimultiples of the same, then the remainders either equal the same or are equimultiples of them.
---
proof:

Let two magnitudes *AB* and *CD* be equimultiples of two magnitudes *E* and *F,* and let *AG* and *CH* subtracted from them be equimultiples of the same two *E* and *F.*

I say that the remainders *GB* and *HD* either equal *E* and *F* or are equimultiples of them.

